Original commit body from b0959ccadcb6cbfb763600ce1eb842dc2d86665c:

erlang.yaml rowed application [set_env, unset_env, load, start, stop,
ensure_started, ensure_all_started] under env_write. set_env/unset_env are
right under the INV-nular credential ruling; the other five were swept in
with them (the WI-jupaf module sweep, two lines below the row where it was
fixed), so starting an application read as writing the environment.

Read in OTP's kernel source, each of the five is a gen_server call into the
application controller process (load_application / start_application /
stop_application -> call(...)), so they move to process_send, the class
gen_server:call already has. The .app file is read inside the controller,
not at the call site, so no fs_read row.

Tested on the shipped io-boundaries command: the five report as
process_send and env_write carries only set_env.

Addresses INV-butiv.

